60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate A, the Mobile Branch, fits the winter data. It reaches the closed roads.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,A solves the bus gap. It brings the service to the outer wards.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,A has proven attendance. The old outreach stops worked. The digitisation project did not.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,A has high running costs. The vehicle line overran. But the grant covers year one.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,A needs drivers. We have them. The repair clinic needs certified tools. We do not.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the cost is high, but the need is higher. The roads close, the people wait.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, yes. The access gap is the biggest problem. A fixes it.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the skills for A are there. The skills for B are not.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, correct. B needs certified tools. We lost the technician. That is a risk.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, C needs facilitators. We have partners. But A needs drivers. We have them.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,D is digital. It misses the people who can't reach the internet. The remote use peaks late.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"D is good, but it doesn't solve the physical access problem. The bus is gone.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,D is the digitisation project. It stalled before. I don't trust it to finish.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,D is cheap to run. But the grant doesn't cover it well. It is a long-term cost.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,D needs scanning skills. We have volunteers. But A needs drivers. We have staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for A. It reaches the people the roads cut off.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for A. It fills the bus gap. It is the only option that works.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I vote for A. The data shows it works. The other options have failed before.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I vote for A. The cost is high, but the need is real. The grant helps.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for A. We have the drivers. We don't have the tool certification.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
